Links fixture: the terminal never opens a link unless the host turns links on.

Visible HTTPS text (the only thing a host may open):
  https://example.com/visible-link
  see https://example.com/docs/terminal.

OSC 8 hidden destination (the label is shown, the target is never read):
  ]8;;https://hidden.example/secret\hidden destination label]8;;\

A path:
  /etc/hosts
  ./notes/readme.md

A command scheme:
  command:workbench.action.openSettings
  vscode://file/etc/hosts

Not HTTPS:
  http://example.com/insecure
  javascript:alert(1)

A download-looking address (visible HTTPS text, so it follows the same rule):
  https://example.com/archive.zip?download=1

